ity across long tasks. Implementing this capability over the standard MCP protocol brings progressive disclosure to any compatible client without native skill engine support.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- more --&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h1 class="relative group"&gt;1. Theoretical Foundation: How MCP and Skills Complement Each Other&#10; &lt;div id="1-theoretical-foundation-how-mcp-and-skills-complement-each-other" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#1-theoretical-foundation-how-mcp-and-skills-complement-each-other" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;1.1 MCP&amp;rsquo;s Characteristics&#10; &lt;div id="11-mcps-characteristics" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#11-mcps-characteristics" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;MCP (Model Context Protocol) is a &amp;ldquo;model-driven tool invocation protocol&amp;rdquo;. Its key characteristics:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>